WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.640
So my name is Graeme Clark, and I'm the director of Ethos Safety.

2
00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:09.480
So Ethos Safety is a full-service health and safety consultancy based in the Highlands of Scotland.

3
00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:14.640
Previously, we'd used paper templates for inspecting or auditing sites,

4
00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:21.120
and that was nothing more complicated than a clipboard and a pre-printed template.

5
00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:24.000
We then moved to using cloud-based software,

6
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:29.040
but we spent quite a lot of time focusing on the iPad, looking at the iPad, scrolling up,

7
00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:35.640
making these ticks in boxes, or physically typing in boxes and taking a photograph for that topic.

8
00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:42.880
So the old method would probably take anywhere from 40 to 60 minutes on the site,

9
00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:48.720
but it did require some degree of administration once you'd left the site.

10
00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:54.440
We used that relatively successfully, and we continued to use that in the business

11
00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:57.440
right up until the point where we adopted Quickler.

12
00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:02.480
We know that all I need to do is snap a couple of photographs, and I do mean snap,

13
00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:08.040
you know, physically go click, click, click, and then think for three or four sentences

14
00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:10.240
and give that to Quickler as a voice note.

15
00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:15.040
It felt almost like we weren't putting enough effort in using Quickler

16
00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:20.760
because it was deceptively easy to capture the data by purely just describing it.

17
00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:27.920
And that is so efficient that we're maybe only spending a fifth, if not a sixth of the time

18
00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:28.960
actually doing the task.

19
00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:33.720
We spend the rest of the remaining time interacting with people, which is what we're there to do.

20
00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:37.040
We're there to actually change people's behaviours on health and safety.

21
00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:42.520
The beauty with Quickler is we actually can see how long it takes to edit the report.

22
00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:47.480
It's taking, on average, between five to 10 minutes,

23
00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:50.960
so there is no requirement to revisit the task.

24
00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:52.880
So it's a one and done, basically.

25
00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:55.840
I wouldn't hesitate to recommend it to anybody else.

26
00:01:55.840 --> 00:02:01.440
Everybody I've ever shown it to almost looks on with a gaze of wonder to say,

27
00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:03.080
oh, how is it doing that?

28
00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:06.400
It's a vital part of what we now do day to day.
